//ERR any
//BUG="a closing bracket with no opener silently truncates the file"

// Not in FEEDBACK.md. `parse_blocks` (src/compiler/preprocessor.rs) returns as
// soon as it sees `)`, `]` or `}` so that a recursive call can hand the
// closer back to its caller. At the top level there is no caller: `preprocess`
// calls `parse_blocks(&fragments, &mut 0)` and throws the index away without
// checking that every fragment was consumed.
//
// So a closing bracket that never had an opener is not an error — it is the
// end of the program. Everything after it is discarded in silence, and the
// compiler exits 0 having built only the part above it. This case compiles
// today and prints "reached"; `dropped_fn` never reaches the parser.
//
// An unclosed opener is reported (00_lexical/54e, 55e) and a mismatched pair
// is reported (00_lexical/60e); only the unmatched closer gets through. The
// fix is for `preprocess` to reject leftover fragments after `parse_blocks`
// returns, pointing at the stray closer.

fn main
    out "reached"
}
fn dropped_fn
    out "dropped"
